  "evidence": "tasks.py:442-452 derives the scheduled window start arithmetically and never passes it through `_floor_to_interval`:\n\n    progress_to = collection_progress_to(\n        last_bucket=last_bucket,\n        watermark=_last_collected_window_to(session, config.id),\n        delta=delta,\n    )\n    ...\n        time_from = min(progress_to, time_to) - delta * SCHEDULED_RESUME_OVERLAP_BUCKETS\n\nThe `watermark` half is new in this branch and is read verbatim out of historical JSON \u2014 tasks.py:196-198: \"the same fact is read back from the window the finished job recorded in ``result_summary[\\\"time_to\\\"]`` \u2014 which a scheduled collection sets to ``floor(now)``, the grid boundary it collected up to.\" On `origin/main` that `floor(now)` was the OLD helper, anchored at 2000-01-01, a Saturday, so every `1w` config's stored `result_summary[\"time_to\"]` is a **Saturday**. Nothing in the branch migrates, re-floors or reconciles those rows; `_last_collected_window_to` (tasks.py:216-237) returns the string parsed as-is.\n\nMeanwhile `_helpers.py:88-107` now promises the opposite for window bounds \u2014 \"MUST agree with :func:`tripl.core.bucketing.floor_to_bucket` for every interval code: these bounds are the window the warehouse's own ``GROUP BY`` is evaluated over, so a bound off the bucket grid splits a bucket across two chunks and lets an incomplete bucket be written as complete\" \u2014 and generation.py:70-79 states \"Boundaries stay interval-aligned because ``time_from``/``time_to`` come from ``_floor_to_interval``/``_ceil_to_interval``\". For the scheduled path `time_from` does not come from either.\n\nRun against the real modules (backend/.venv/bin/python), weekly config, pre-deploy job recorded `time_to=2026-09-05` (Saturday), newest stored bucket 2026-08-24 (Monday), tick at 2026-09-14T00:05Z:\n    progress_to: 2026-09-05 Saturday\n    time_to:     2026-09-14 Monday\n    time_from:   2026-08-22 Saturday | on grid? False\n    warehouse bucket key for the leading days: 2026-08-17 -> below time_from\n    days of that week inside the window: 2 of 7\n\nmetric_rows.py:473-477 deletes only `bucket >= time_from AND bucket < time_to`, so 2026-08-17 is NOT deleted; metric_rows.py:304-320 then upserts it with `set_={\"count\": excluded.count}` \u2014 a blind overwrite. chunk_processing.py:282 takes the bucket straight from the warehouse row with no range filter.\n\nwebsite/docs/run/runbook.md:600-608 tells operators the opposite: \"This release measures the window from the same Monday origin the buckets use, so a weekly window now opens and closes on a Monday\" followed by \"What to expect after the deploy, without doing anything.\"",
  "failure_scenario": "A `1w` scan config, source silent since Mon 2026-08-31. Stored EventMetric weekly buckets 2026-08-17 (complete, e.g. count 700) and 2026-08-24 (complete). Newest completed dispatcher job was written before this branch and recorded `result_summary[\"time_to\"] = \"2026-09-05T00:00:00+00:00\"` (Saturday, old 2000-01-01 anchor). First post-deploy tick at 2026-09-14T00:05Z: `progress_to = max(2026-08-24+1w, 2026-09-05) = 2026-09-05`, `time_to = 2026-09-14`, so `time_from = 2026-08-22` \u2014 a Saturday, off the Monday grid. The warehouse's `toMonday`/`WEEK(MONDAY)` GROUP BY over [2026-08-22, 2026-09-14) returns bucket key 2026-08-17 holding only Sat 08-22 + Sun 08-23 (2 of 7 days, e.g. count 190). That key is below `time_from`, so `_delete_event_metrics_window` leaves the existing row alone, and `_upsert_event_metrics_rows` then overwrites count 700 with 190. The detector's evaluation window (`time_to - 30 * delta`) covers 2026-08-17 and the bucket is in `covered_buckets` (it has a stored row), so a ~73% drop is scored as a MetricAnomaly and alerts fire. Every later run has a Monday-aligned `progress_to`, so `time_from` never reaches 2026-08-17 again and the corrupted point is permanent. With `replay_chunk_interval` set the damage is worse: `_iter_window_chunks` steps 1w from the Saturday start, so bucket 2026-08-24 is split across chunks [08-22,08-29) and [08-29,09-05); the second chunk's delete (`bucket >= 08-29`) does not cover 08-24 and its upsert overwrites the full week with the Sat+Sun tail \u2014 exactly the last-chunk-wins corruption tripl-0zpq.10 claims to have eliminated.",
