  "evidence": "ReplayDialog.tsx:44-50 seeds the end at the client's own floor of the current instant:\n\n    const to = new Date(getBucketStart(new Date().toISOString(), granularity))\n\nThe backend accepts only `time_to <= floor_to_bucket(server now, interval)` \u2014 scan_service.py:450-451:\n\n    latest_complete = floor_to_bucket(datetime.now(UTC), config.interval)\n    if data.time_to > latest_complete:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, ...)\n\nThe seeded value is the largest value the check accepts, so any positive client-vs-server clock skew that straddles a bucket boundary makes the dialog's own default illegal. The replaced code (`to.setMinutes(0, 0, 0)`) put the boundary on the hour instead, so for a `15m` config the exposed span goes from the last N minutes of each hour to the last N minutes of every 15 minutes.",
  "failure_scenario": "A scan config with `interval: '15m'`. The user's browser clock is 2 minutes fast (ordinary drift on a laptop without NTP). Real UTC is 2026-09-12T14:28:30; the browser reports 14:30:30, so `defaultReplayWindow` seeds `to = 2026-09-12T14:30:00Z`. The user opens Replay and presses \"Replay period\" without editing anything. `trigger_metrics_replay` computes `latest_complete = floor_to_bucket(14:28:30, '15m') = 14:15:00Z`, and `14:30 > 14:15`, so the request is rejected: HTTP 400 \"Replay period must end at or before 2026-09-12 14:15 UTC: the current 15m interval has not finished, so it holds no complete bucket to replay.\" This lands for roughly the last 2 minutes of every 15-minute bucket (~13% of attempts) instead of the last 2 minutes of every hour (~3%) under the old seed.",
  "fix": "Seed one bucket behind the client's floor rather than on it \u2014 `to = getBucketStart(now) - bucketWidth` (the width is already computed on line 48 as `to - previous`), keeping `from` at least 24h earlier. That costs the user one bucket of default range and makes the default immune to sub-interval clock skew. Alternatively return the acceptable boundary from the API (e.g. on the ScanConfig read) and seed from that instead of from the browser clock."
