  "evidence": "event_plan.py:750-760, now reached from the metric collector for every row:\n\n```\n    for col_name, idx in json_index.items():\n        if col_name in (event_type_column, time_column):\n            continue\n        paths = row[n_reg + idx]\n        ...\n        for full_path, value_idx in json_value_index.items():\n            if full_path.startswith(f\"{col_name}.\"):\n                values[full_path] = format_json_path_value(row[value_idx])\n```\n\n`format_json_path_value` -> `decode_json_path_value` does `json.loads(raw_value)` on every string (json_paths.py:50-55), so this is one json.loads per (JSON column x declared path) per row, unconditional.\n\nThe code it replaced in metric_rows.py only touched the paths the row actually carried (removed in this diff):\n\n```\n-                    raw_values_by_field[full_path] = format_json_path_value(\n-                        data_row[json_value_index[full_path]]\n-                    )\n```\n\n...inside `for path in sorted_paths:`.\n\nmetric_rows.py:78-86 calls it once per row, and the call site is reached three times per chunk \u2014 chunk_processing.py:318, metric_rows.py:845 (_collect_metric_breakdown_rows) and metric_rows.py:997 (_collect_app_version_breakdown_rows). Two more row-independent recomputations sit in the same per-row body: metric_rows.py:152 `event_name_format_columns(event_name_format)` and metric_rows.py:158 `json_name_format_keys(event_name_format, col_meta)`, both regex scans. plan_events hoists exactly these out of its loop and says why \u2014 event_plan.py:515-518: \"Both are row-independent, so they are derived once.\"\n\nChunk size is metrics_row_limit, default 100_000 (config.py:220), and replay widens json_value_names up to 200 paths per JSON column (generation.py:148 `_MAX_REPLAY_JSON_PATHS_PER_COLUMN = 200`, applied by _augment_json_value_paths_for_replay_tokens).",
