  "fix": "Hoist the row-independent work to the caller and index the paths by column once. Precompute `paths_by_column: dict[str, list[tuple[str, int]]]` (full_path -> row index, grouped by base column) plus `name_columns` and `json_format_keys` once per chunk and pass them into raw_values_from_row / _build_event_name_from_row, instead of rebuilding json_value_index, re-scanning every json_value_name with startswith, and re-running the two regex helpers on every row. Inside the loop, read only the paths that column owns, and skip format_json_path_value for a value column the row's path list does not mention (matching what the pre-change collector did)."
