  "evidence": "backend/src/tripl/worker/tasks/scan.py:83-88\n```\n# Statuses from which a job must never be resurrected by the worker. ``running``\n# is deliberately absent: with ``task_acks_late`` a redelivered message\n# legitimately re-enters its own running job. Spelled out here rather than\n# imported from ``worker.tasks.metrics._helpers`` \u2014 that import would pull the\n# whole ``collect_metrics`` task graph into this module's import path \u2014 but it\n# means the same thing as its twin there and must stay in step with it.\n_TERMINAL_BEFORE_START = (ScanJobStatus.cancelled.value, ScanJobStatus.failed.value)\n```\nThe twin, backend/src/tripl/worker/tasks/metrics/_helpers.py:55-59:\n```\nTERMINAL_SCAN_JOB_STATUSES = (\n    ScanJobStatus.completed.value,\n    ScanJobStatus.failed.value,\n    ScanJobStatus.cancelled.value,\n)\n```\nand its own rationale at _helpers.py:48-52: \"Terminal means somebody else already closed the row \u2014 the user cancelled it, the stale reaper stamped it failed, **or its completed ack was lost**\". `completed` is absent from `_TERMINAL_BEFORE_START`, so the two do not mean the same thing. `task_acks_late = True` is global (backend/src/tripl/worker/celery_app.py:46). The guard that uses it, scan.py:523-532, is commented \"See ``run_scan``: a stopped or reaped job must not be resurrected by an ``acks_late`` redelivery, and this pass DELETES the events it folds.\"",
  "failure_scenario": "`apply_event_groups` finishes, writes `job.status = completed` (scan.py:616) and commits, then the worker is SIGKILLed / the broker connection drops before the ack lands. Under `task_acks_late` RabbitMQ redelivers the same message. `job.status` is now `\"completed\"`, which is not in `_TERMINAL_BEFORE_START`, so the guard at scan.py:526 does not fire: the task flips the row back to `running`, re-runs `merge_existing_events_for_group_rules` over the already-folded catalog (deleting events again), re-runs the reindex and re-stamps `completed`. The metrics twin refuses exactly this case. Same hole in `run_scan` (scan.py:198): a redelivered completed catalog scan re-executes the warehouse query and rewrites the plan.",
  "fix": "Either add `ScanJobStatus.completed.value` to `_TERMINAL_BEFORE_START` so it really is the twin of `TERMINAL_SCAN_JOB_STATUSES`, or correct the comment to say that `completed` is deliberately excluded and why."
