  "evidence": "backend/src/tripl/services/scan_service.py:529-535:\n```\n    running task is not killed; it stops cooperatively at its next checkpoint,\n    and every scan task has one: a metrics collection or replay polls this status\n    at each chunk boundary and keeps what it already wrote, while a catalog run\n    or an event-group apply re-reads it before it commits and therefore writes\n    nothing at all. Either way the job stays ``cancelled`` and never turns itself\n    back into ``completed``.\n```\nwebsite/docs/run/cli.md:903: \"... a catalog run or an event-group apply before its write commits, so it writes nothing at all. **A stopped job stays `cancelled`.**\"\n\nThe catalog tasks check the cancel exactly once, before their commit (scan.py:318, scan.py:597), and unconditionally stamp success afterwards:\n```\nbackend/src/tripl/worker/tasks/scan.py:345-347\n        # Mark job as completed\n        job.status = ScanJobStatus.completed.value\n        job.completed_at = datetime.now(UTC)\n```\n```\nbackend/src/tripl/worker/tasks/scan.py:616-617\n        job.status = ScanJobStatus.completed.value\n        job.completed_at = datetime.now(UTC)\n```\nThere is no `_closed_by_someone_else` equivalent on either path \u2014 unlike `collect_metrics`, which does re-check (tasks.py:1194-1210). The same commit's own user doc states the opposite behaviour at website/docs/use/feature-reference.md:1370-1371: \"Stopped after that \u2014 while the run is retiring variables or rebuilding the search index \u2014 their work is already durable and the run finishes as *Succeeded*.\"",
  "failure_scenario": "A catalog scan on a large project passes the checkpoint at scan.py:318 and commits, then spends time in `retire_unused_variables` and `reindex_main_branch_from_worker` (scan.py:336-343). During that window the user presses **Stop run** (or `tripl scans cancel`): `cancel_scan_job` sets `status = cancelled` in the request session and returns. `run_scan` then executes scan.py:346 and commits `status = completed`. The run row reads **Succeeded**, the CLI table and the API docstring both said it would stay `cancelled`.",
  "fix": "Either re-read the status before the final stamp on both catalog paths (the `_closed_by_someone_else` pattern `collect_metrics` already uses), or reword scan_service.py:534-535 and cli.md:903 to match feature-reference.md:1370-1371 \u2014 cancellation is honoured only up to the pre-commit checkpoint."
